{"availability":"available","full":"logisky/LogiSheets","name":"LogiSheets","description":"LogiSheets is an AI-friendly spreadsheet application that is compatible with Excel and a good place where human and AI work together.","category":"AI & machine learning","language":"TypeScript","stars":276,"forks":10,"created":"2022-01-19T02:16:56Z","updated":"2026-10-09T07:37:34Z","license":null,"branch":"main","homepage":"https://www.logisheets.com/","topics":["agents-sdk","ai","ai-native","awesome","compute-engine","datagrid","excel","googlesheets","grid","ooxml-workbooks","react","reactjs","rust","spreadsheet","structured-data","svelte","tauri","typescript","wasm","xlsx"],"demo":"https://www.logisheets.com/?craft=factory-simulator","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T19:51:38.198Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-11T19:51:38.198Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-11T19:51:38.198Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-11T19:51:38.198Z","stars":276,"forks":10}],"technologies":["React","Svelte","Rust"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["The spreadsheet as common ground for people and AI. LogiSheets is a web-based spreadsheet built on a Rust engine compiled to WebAssembly — it reads, manipulates, and writes real .xlsx files, and runs the same engine in the browser and on Node. What makes it different is who it's built for: both the person looking at the grid and the agent operating on it.","A spreadsheet is the most widely understood interface humans have for structured data, and one of the worst interfaces a machine could be handed. Everything that makes a sheet readable to a person is invisible to a model — the extent of a table is a visual convention, the header row is a habit, and what column D means lives in somebody's head. So an AI given a spreadsheet guesses at coordinates and writes plausible cells that are wrong in ways nobody notices until much later.","LogiSheets closes that gap in the document itself. Blocks give regions a stable identity and a schema, so an agent addresses data as (block, field, key) rather than Sheet1!C5. Declarations, rules, and write policies live in the file — the engine can tell an agent what a column means, when a value is wrong, and which cells it may not touch. The human still sees an ordinary grid, and the file is still a real .xlsx."],"features":["One engine, everywhere. The core spreadsheet engine is written in Rust and compiled to WASM. The exact same logic powers the browser app and a headless Node runtime — no reimplementation, no drift.","Real Excel files. Read and write .xlsx with formulas, styles, and structure preserved.","Structured data (Blocks). A Block keeps a region of cells together as a coherent, schema-aware table — cells are addressed by stable IDs, so inserts and deletes never break references. Fields carry types, validation…","Legible to an agent. A block is a noun an AI can name, with fields it can read the meaning of and records it can address by key. Whatever an agent declares, it can read back — the state is in the file, not in a prompt.","Wrong is visible, not silent. The engine generates validation from the declaration and reports every cell that currently fails it, so a mistake surfaces as data an agent can act on instead of a number that merely looks…"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/logisky/LogiSheets/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"eca2af627565b3813f693bdfe5262e7ec3b1d2d0cc6d20d5d637b1cd690a1c76","extractedAt":"2026-10-11T19:51:38.349Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T19:51:38.349Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"The spreadsheet as common ground for people and AI. LogiSheets is a web-based spreadsheet built on a Rust engine compiled to WebAssembly — it reads, manipulates, and writes real .xlsx files, and runs the same engine in the browser and on Node. What makes it different is who it's built for: both the person looking at the grid and the agent operating on it.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/logisky/LogiSheets/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[{"text":"The spreadsheet as common ground for people and AI. LogiSheets is a web-based spreadsheet built on a Rust engine compiled to WebAssembly — it reads, manipulates, and writes real .xlsx files, and runs the same engine in the browser and on Node. What makes it different is who it's built for: both the person looking at the grid and the agent operating on it.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/logisky/LogiSheets/blob/main/README.md"}],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"eca2af627565b3813f693bdfe5262e7ec3b1d2d0cc6d20d5d637b1cd690a1c76","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/logisky/LogiSheets/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-11T19:51:38.349Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-09T07:37:34Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/logisky/LogiSheets/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-11T19:51:38.350Z","hash":"eca2af627565b3813f693bdfe5262e7ec3b1d2d0cc6d20d5d637b1cd690a1c76","originalBytes":10019,"storedBytes":10019,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["engine","agent","core","logisheets","node","packages","crafts","spreadsheet","what","browser","web","app","block","every","live","logic","same","write","xlsx","api","blocks","craft","data","one","person","read","real","runtime","rust","wasm","watson","both","built","cell","cells","craftsmith","docs","grid","host","license","logician","see","tool","workbook","column","definitions","desktop","extension","field","file","formula","formulas","give","headless","logisheets-core","logisheets-web","mit","never","over","plain","reads","rules","runs","surface","to.","toolkit","types","why","wrappers","written","wrong","address","ai.","any","assistant","boundaries","build","carry","check","cli","compiled","context","crates","currently","declared","declares","docs.logisheets.com","document","documentation","engine-neutral","excel","expose","extend","fails","fields","game","generates","host.","human","implementation","interactive","javascript","keeps","let","lives